<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Scandinavian Quarterly, an independent online magazine of Nordic literature and culture.">
<article class="standard-page"><header class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">The Scandinavian Quarterly</p><h1>About the magazine</h1></header><div class="gh-content"><p>The Scandinavian Quarterly is an independent online magazine of Nordic literature and culture. We publish fiction, poetry, essays, criticism, literary translation, interviews, art and photography.</p><p>Our centre of gravity is the Nordic region, but our doors are not closed at its borders. We are interested in work that travels: between languages, countries, traditions and forms.</p><p><strong>TSQ is free to read.</strong> Published work is available online without a subscription or paywall.</p><h2>What we publish</h2><p>Fiction, poetry, essays and criticism, translation, interviews, art and photography that belong in conversation with contemporary Nordic literature and culture.</p><h2>Publication model</h2><p><strong>TSQ is an online-only publication.</strong> We do not publish a print edition. New work appears on the website, and selected work may also be gathered into seasonal online issues and collections.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For submissions, write to <a href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com">submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com</a>. For editorial information, see our <a href="/masthead/">masthead</a> and <a href="/submission-guidelines/">submission guidelines</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
